# .env.example — V1 web-app container (root surface).
#
# Per-surface secret confinement (Phase 5 Step 8; Sec joint-review surface,
# ADR-011 secrets territory). This file enumerates ONLY the secrets the V1
# web-app container is permitted to hold per ARCH §5 "Credentials / secrets
# surface → V1 web-app container". Enumerating ONLY this surface's secrets IS
# the security property — a secret not listed here does not belong in this
# container.
#
# Anchors (verified verbatim 2026-06-28):
#   - ARCH §5 Deployment Topology → V1 web-app container env-var scope.
#   - SECURITY RT-26 — SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY confined to allowlisted §4.1
#     server-source surfaces (3 surfaces per ADR-016 D1); CI fence-rt26 audits.
#   - SECURITY SD-20 — PDF_WORKER_SIGNING_KEY signs/verifies the short-lived PDF
#     worker JWT (RT-21 battery).
#   - ADR-002 §6.0 — canonical secrets discipline (gitignored .env + Coolify
#     env-var injection in production). Real values live ONLY in Coolify, never
#     in the repo. Placeholders below.
#
# Secret-store assignment: ALL values below are PRODUCTION-ONLY (Coolify-injected
# on cax21). See secrets-manifest.yml — none of these names may appear in the
# CI-only set (blast-radius containment).
#
# ⚠ PROHIBITED VARIABLE — `PGTZ` MUST NEVER BE SET HERE OR IN COOLIFY.
#   This is a correctness prohibition, not a secrets one, so the "enumerates only
#   permitted secrets" property above does NOT cover it — hence stating it.
#   MEASURED 2026-08-04: libpq sends PGTZ as a startup parameter that OVERRIDES the
#   database-level TimeZone pin (pg_settings.source becomes `client`). The app derives
#   every NAV as-of date as UTC in the Node process while Postgres evaluates
#   `closed_at::date` in the SESSION zone — a PGTZ here silently desynchronises those
#   two clocks and a just-closed account lingers in the §2.1.1 NAV headline for up to a
#   day, with nothing erroring. See deployment-runbook §4.1 + §10 TZ-1.
#   `TZ` is NOT the same thing and is harmless to the DB session — do not "fix" this by
#   setting TZ=UTC and assuming the database followed. It does not.

# Supabase anon (publishable) key — client-side surface; always present.
SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=<supabase-anon-key>

# Supabase service_role key — RT-26-allowlisted §4.1 server-source surfaces ONLY
# (Plaid webhook / onboard / revoke +server.ts per ADR-016 D1). Never imported
# outside the allowlist; fence-rt26 fails closed at PR-time on any other usage.
SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY=<supabase-service-role-key>

# PDF worker JWT signing key — V1 web-app signs the short-lived (60s + nonce)
# /internal/pdf-render JWT with this; verifies inbound PDF worker calls (SD-20 /
# RT-21). The PDF worker holds the SAME key (its only secret) — see
# workers/pdf-render/.env.example.
PDF_WORKER_SIGNING_KEY=<pdf-worker-signing-key>

# Plaid API credentials (outbound Items / Transactions / Investments; Plaid Link).
PLAID_CLIENT_ID=<plaid-client-id>
PLAID_SECRET=<plaid-secret>

# NOTE: Plaid webhook verification is asymmetric (ES256/JWK) — the worker fetches
# Plaid's public verification key at /webhook_verification_key and verifies the
# inbound JWT signature (RT-05 critical). There is NO static webhook HMAC secret;
# a `PLAID_WEBHOOK_SECRET` env var would gate nothing, so none is declared here.

# Discord webhook URL — outbound notification dispatch (incumbent Coolify→Discord
# routing; reference_coolify_discord_notifications). The web-app surface of the
# F4 notification target; Sec-consult on F1 PII-vector verification is a Phase 5
# detail item per ARCH §4 Observability row.
DISCORD_WEBHOOK_URL=<discord-webhook-url>

# Worker admission shared secret (SELF-212 Option-C, C6-2). The api/ relay tier
# authenticates its POST to the provider-sync worker's INTERNAL admission endpoint
# with this. SAME value on the provider-sync worker (see
# workers/provider-sync/.env.example) — like PDF_WORKER_SIGNING_KEY is shared with
# the PDF worker. 256-bit (`openssl rand -hex 32`); Coolify project-scoped SHARED
# var (single rotation edit point). NOT the service_role key — RT-26 allowlist
# UNCHANGED. Constant-time compare, fail-closed on absent/mismatch (Sec CA-6).
# NB: this is a SERVER secret — it belongs on THIS (server) surface, NEVER in
# api/.env.example (which is PUBLIC_-prefixed browser-exposed vars only).
WORKER_ADMISSION_SHARED_SECRET=<worker-admission-shared-secret>

# Worker admission base URL (SELF-212 Option-C transport target). The api/ relay
# (server-source `src/lib/server/plaid/admissionClient.ts`) POSTs to this base URL
# to reach the provider-sync worker's INTERNAL admission endpoint. NOT a secret —
# it is the internal Docker-network address — so it is intentionally NOT a
# secrets-manifest entry; declared here as a server-tier env contract (default in
# code if unset). Default `http://provider-sync:8081` = the worker's Coolify
# service name (`provider-sync` container) + ADMISSION_PORT (8081); these MUST
# match workers/provider-sync/docker-compose.yaml. Server-only — never browser-
# exposed (NOT in api/.env.example PUBLIC_ surface). Same-project reach per CA-4.
WORKER_ADMISSION_URL=http://provider-sync:8081   # non-secret (internal URL)

# --- NOT secrets / out of scope for this file --------------------------------
# Non-secret SvelteKit client config (e.g. the Supabase project URL, PUBLIC_*
# prefixed vars) is NOT enumerated here — it is not a credential and is not part
# of the secret-confinement contract. It lands with the SvelteKit scaffold in
# Phase 6 (this root package.json is a Husky hook host only, not the app
# manifest). Adding a NEW secret to this surface is an ARCH §5 change → DevOps +
# Sec joint-review.
